 name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='4'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='5'><run><font size='11pt' style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable'
 truetype='true' familyid='20'/>The Budget (Green): </run><run><font size='11pt'
 name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>the Administrator can adjust the limit of each sub-budget: Operating, Travel, Conract and Capital.  These amounts are used to verify that limits are not exceeded when the buttons [Save], [Mail to Admin], or [Got it] are used on an order.</run></par>
<par def='4'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='5'><run><font size='11pt' style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable'
 truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Committed (Blue):</run><run><font size='11pt'
 name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/> the committed amounts are calculated each time the budget for an order belonging to that project is calculated.  The Budget for a specific order is calculated only one time and it occurs when the Administrator clicks on the button [On Order].  If the Administrator click on the button [Re-Calculate Budget] in the Project form, the committed amounts are re-calculated using only the Orders for which the button "On Order" have been used in the past.  When an order is cancelled, the committed amount is reduced.</run></par>
<pardef id='8' leftmargin='1.2500in' rightmargin='100%' firstlineleftmargin='1in'
 tabs='L1in L1.5000in L1.7500in L2.2500in L2.7500in L3.2500in L3.7500in L4.2500in L4.7500in L5.2500in L5.7500in'/>
<par def='8'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/></run></par>
<pardef id='9' leftmargin='1.2500in' rightmargin='100%' tabs='L1in L1.5000in L1.7500in L2.2500in L2.7500in L3.2500in L3.7500in L4.2500in L4.7500in L5.2500in L5.7500in'/>
<par def='9'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>- Situation #1: When the project </run><run><font size='11pt'
 style='underline' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>is exempted from GST and when there is no Exchange Rate</run><run
><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>, the cost added to the committed amount in the project is:</run></par>
<pardef id='10' leftmargin='1.5000in' rightmargin='100%' tabs='L1in L1.5000in L1.7500in L2.2500in L2.7500in L3.2500in L3.7500in L4.2500in L4.7500in L5.2500in L5.7500in'/>
<par def='10'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>(Total Price of all items to purchase + Shipping fees + Customs fees)</run></par>
<par def='9'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>- Situation #2: When the project</run><run><font size='11pt'
 style='underline' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/> is exempted from GST and when there is an Exchange Rate</run><run
><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>, the cost added to the committed amount in the project is:</run></par>
<par def='10'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>(Total Price of all items to purchase + Shipping fees + Customs fees) + Exchange Rate * (Total Price of all items to purchase + Shipping fees + Customs fees)</run></par>
<par def='9'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>- Situation #3: When the project </run><run><font size='11pt'
 style='underline' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>is not exempted from GST and when there is no Exchange Rate</run><run
><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>, the cost added to the committed amount in the project is:</run></par>
<par def='10'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>(Total Price of all items to purchase + Shipping fees + Customs fees) * GST</run></par>
<par def='9'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>- Situation #4: When the project </run><run><font size='11pt'
 style='underline' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>is not exempted from GST and when there is an Exchange Rate</run><run
><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/>, the cost added to the committed amount in the project is:</run></par>
<par def='10'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>((Total Price of all items to purchase + Shipping fees + Customs fees) + Exchange Rate * (Total Price of all items to purchase + Shipping fees + Customs fees)) * GST</run></par>
<par def='4'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/></run></par>
<pardef id='11' leftmargin='1.2500in' list='bullet' tabs='L0.5000in L1in L1.5000in L2in L2.5000in L3in L3.5000in L4in'/>
<par def='11'><run><font size='11pt' style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable'
 truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Total Budget (Pink):</run><run><font size='11pt'
 name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/> This is the sum of the Operation, Travel, Contract and Capital budgets.  This amount is automatically calculated by the system.  This amount is used to verify that the budget limits is not exceeded when the buttons [Save], [Mail to Admin], or [Got it] are used on an order.</run></par>
<pardef id='12' leftmargin='1in' tabs='L0.5000in L1in L1.5000in L2in L2.5000in L3in L3.5000in L4in'/>
<par def='12'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='11'><run><font size='11pt' style='bold' name='Arial' pitch='variable'
 truetype='true' familyid='20'/>Total Committed (Grey):</run><run><font size='11pt'
 name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true' familyid='20'/> This is the sum of the committed amounts for Operation, Travel, Contract and Capital budgets.  This amount is automatically calculated by the system.</run></par>
<par def='12'><run><font size='11pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
